body.translated_text:
Whatever is a mind connects to another mind [in a subsequent moment];
just as the present mind;
and the mind exists at the time of death — this is the natural reason (<s>svabhāvahetu</s>).

Therefore the following argument should be formulated:
The <s>Buddha</s>'s eye does not have past and future objects as its domain;
because it is an eye;
like our own eye.
Or [alternatively]: it is not an eye at all;
because it has past and future objects as its domain;
like sound.
(Nibandh 8)
